%% @fig 04
%% @kicker The context switching tax
%% @alt An engineer working in the IDE needs an answer. Documentation kept in the same repository answers it a few keystrokes away, so the engineer stays in flow. A question sent to Slack or a stale wiki page pulls the engineer out of the IDE and drops the mental state they were holding.
%% @caption Docs that live next to the code put answers at the point of need. Every detour to Slack or a wiki costs a cognitive restart.
%% @path ide>docs
%% @glyph ide | window
%% @glyph docs | doc check
%% @glyph slack | reader question
%% @glyph wiki | doc cross
flowchart LR
  ide["IDE"]:::accent
  docs["Docs in repo"]:::focal
  slack["Slack"]:::muted
  wiki["Wiki"]:::muted
  ide --> docs
  ide -.-> slack
  ide -.-> wiki
